Package: scdRs
Title: Single-Cell Disease-Relevance Score
Version: 0.99.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Sina", "Ravanbakhsh", email = "rav.sina@gmail.com",
        role = c("aut", "cre"),
        comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0002-9624-1898")),
    person("Martin Jinye", "Zhang", role = "cph",
        comment = "Author of the original Python scDRS"),
    person("Kangcheng", "Hou", role = "cph",
        comment = "Author of the original Python scDRS"))
Description: A native R implementation of scDRS (single-cell
    disease-relevance score; Zhang, Hou et al., Nature Genetics 2022).
    scDRS links single-cell RNA-seq data to polygenic disease risk by
    scoring each cell for excess expression of a GWAS-derived disease
    gene set relative to matched control gene sets, and provides
    downstream tests for cell-type association and heterogeneity.
    The package works on SingleCellExperiment objects.
